  "review": {
    "note": "Admit Core 0.45 while retaining the verified 0.43/0.44 public ingest facade and schema-9 contracts; the next unverified 0.46 compatibility lane remains excluded. Core 0.45.0 wheel SHA256 255180d5bd152b4744a6f3932f354e110e6b621c86f211854978780089ffc8ba installed with normal dependency resolution, without --no-deps. Core 0.43.0, 0.44.0 and 0.45.0 each passed 33 focused package, logging, source-probe and real SQLite runtime cases; 0.45 additionally passed all 33 selected MariaDB 10.11.11 resident e2e, process recovery and progress cases (676.27s). Schema-2 query attribution is not an ingest data-format change: the probe consumes unchanged exact operation counters, verified against both log schemas. Registry Core 0.44.0 remains supported; unpublished 0.45 is supplied explicitly for this release. Other registry candidates match the preceding audit except Hypothesis 6.168.3. Its official changelog (https://hypothesis.readthedocs.io/en/latest/changelog.html) fixes quadratic pytest statistics summarization above 100k cases; installed 6.168.3 passed all 3 incremental property tests. No database, journal, CBZ/artwork or runtime facade conversion is needed. Exact final-tree merge gate and clean installed-wheel smoke are separate evidence.",
